      "summaryMarkdown": "Full re-review after the owner's epic amendment (`nsh-root` becomes a read-only reference, PR texts move to `gpuitizen:docs/pr/**`), which invalidated the stored review; the s1 criteria, tasks, checks and product source are unchanged since my reattested pass. Nothing in s1 depends on nsh-root: both tasks map only to `gpuitizen` paths, and no s1 file references `nsh-root`, `upstream-pr` or `docs/upstream`. README.md lists exactly the four execution repositories of the amended d01, and AGENTS.md keeps the no-NSH rule. WS-1/TGT-4: the workspace, pins, lints, release profile, toolchain, alias and licences comply, and `policy::tests` fails on each drift. TGT-1: both specs are correct (armv7 softfp with +v7,+thumb2,+vfp3,+neon, vendor tizen, 32-bit; x86_64 vendor tizen), and `targets::tests` checks the fields and that the pinned nightly accepts both. TGT-2: `cross::tests` covers the command lines and environment for both targets: build-std, the json spec, clang --target/--sysroot plus the armv7 flags, clang+lld linking via gcc-ld, the pinned RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN, clippy with -D warnings, passthrough, --all-tv-libs, the early missing-rootstrap failure for linking builds only, inherited RUSTFLAGS merged into CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS, and --check-symbols rejected before Cargo. WS-2: AGENTS.md matches the workspace. Both earlier findings stay resolved. Risk to confirm at the first real link in s3: the x86_64 default rootstrap name `tizen-8.0-emulator64.core`.",
